Page links for a long list, with the current page highlighted.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/pagination)

<%= embed AppicaUI::PaginationPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Pagination do
  PaginationPages(page: @page, pages: @pages) { |page| posts_path(page:) }
end
```

`PaginationPages` builds the usual row for page `page:` of `pages:`: previous, the first and last pages, a `window:`
of pages around the current one with ellipses for the gaps, and next - disabled at the ends. It works with any
paginator (Pagy, Kaminari, `limit`/`offset`), since you only pass numbers and a URL block. The parts are Appica's
primitives, so you can also lay a row out yourself:

```ruby
Pagination do
  PaginationList do
    PaginationItem { PaginationLink(href: "?page=1", active: true) { "1" } }
    PaginationItem { PaginationLink(href: "?page=2") { "2" } }
    PaginationItem { PaginationEllipsis() }
    PaginationItem { PaginationLink(href: "?page=10") { "10" } }
  end
end
```

