## API reference

### Pagination

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:outline`, `:soft` | `:outline` | Link style for every link. |
| `size:` | `:sm`, `:md`, `:lg` | `:md` | Link size for every link. |
| `aria_label:` | `String` | "Pagination" | The landmark's name (translated). |

### PaginationPages

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `page:` / `pages:` | `Integer` | - | The current page and the page count. |
| `window:` | `Integer` | `1` | Pages shown on each side of the current one. |
| `edges:` | `Boolean` | `false` | First / last jumps. |
| block | `\|page\| url` | - | The URL of a page. |

### PaginationLink

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `active:` | `Boolean` | `false` | The current page: filled, `aria-current="page"`, not clickable. |
| `disabled:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Dimmed and out of the tab order (out-of-range previous / next). |
| `icon:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Square around a lone icon - add an `aria_label:`. |

A block that takes an argument receives the attributes for your own element. `PaginationList` is the `<ul>`,
`PaginationItem` an `<li>`, `PaginationEllipsis` the "…" (with a screen-reader-only "More pages").

## Accessibility

- A `<nav>` landmark named "Pagination"; the current page is `aria-current="page"`.
- Page links are labelled "Go to page N", previous / next / first / last are named (translated) and disabled at the
  ends with `aria-disabled`.
- The ellipsis is hidden from assistive tech apart from its "More pages" text.
